{"title":"2013 Mock AIME I Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Mock_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In a magic circuit, there are six lights in a series, and if one of the lights short circuit, then all lights after it will short circuit as well, without affecting the lights before it. Once a turn, a random light that isn’t already short circuited is short circuited. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the expected number of turns it takes to short circuit all of the lights, find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/9/3796ffdb09e156a707f9fe32d25d464dd4b9d1a8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100E$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Mock_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/3/0d3cbf9ab1e976e485e5a8b8459491ffa0b561dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"21\" height=\"15\" /> be the expected value of turns it takes to short circuit <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> lights. Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/c/3cc2b5320320a449292eee94231cea2018885cf3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E_1=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"53\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/d/50d7d051ce7836eb1c77930b63e6cfabee300cef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E_2=\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}(E_1+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"158\" height=\"37\" />, and in general, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/8/bc8e35e3de47d4ea6ade02c84b96345668239991.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[E_k=\\frac{1}{k}+\\frac{1}{k}(E_{k-1}+1)+\\frac{1}{k}(E_{k-2}+1)+\\dots+\\frac{1}{k}(E_1+1)=1+\\frac{1}{k}(\\sum_{i=1}^{k-1} E_i)\\]\" width=\"511\" height=\"50\" /> Doing that calculations gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/4/2c4cfcb00b6ad431d9194938cd376c0e3dfe135a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E_6=\\frac{49}{20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"65\" height=\"37\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/4/b64abf8d730a7ac2061f60d337b116fa68bed70c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100E_6=\\boxed{245}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"111\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Mock_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Mock_AIME_I_Problems\" title=\"2013 Mock AIME I Problems\">2013 Mock AIME I Problems</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Mock_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2013 Mock AIME I Problems/Problem 8\">Preceded by Problem 8</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2013_Mock_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2013 Mock AIME I Problems/Problem 10\">Followed by Problem 10</a></li></ul>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached